{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "0525e6ee-5e99-4f34-be06-40d857f9fbab",
    "name": "notification-service",
    "description": "Device registration and the notification inbox.\n\nOwner: dan1el50. Port: 8084 (reached through the gateway on 8080).\n\nEverything goes through the API Gateway (`{{gatewayUrl}}`): players register and log in at User Management through it, and the gateway verifies their token and forwards requests with `X-User-Id` + `X-Gateway-Key` instead. The service accepts nothing else - the `... without the gateway` request shows the 401. Each run registers new players (`{{runId}}`), so it can be run repeatedly.\n\nNotifications have no HTTP create endpoint: they only exist once a service publishes an event on the `notification-events` Redis channel. A fresh player's inbox is therefore empty, and `Mark my notification as read` is skipped. To see it run, publish an event for `{{playerId}}` between the two requests (README, Events Consumed) and run the collection from `List my notifications`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "38273956"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gatewayUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "notificationUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8084",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Secret123!",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "invalidToken",
      "value": "not-a-real-token",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "runId",
      "value": "",
